  "summary": "A macOS Apple Silicon infostealer chain that shows a deceptive AppleScript \"Password Request\" dialog via /usr/bin/osascript, validates the harvested password with dscl . authonly, and installs a LaunchDaemon for persistence. It stages Keychain, Safari cookie, Notes, SSH and shell-history files under /tmp/lksopo, compresses them with ditto, exfiltrates the archive via curl POST to 109.238.87.111, and downloads a second-stage bot from 193.178.159.129 before deleting the staging directory. Hidden state files (~/.bhost, ~/.phost, ~/.username, ~/.pwd) written by the first stage are required by the dropped bot.",
